takeaways=[
 ('Operational measures:','Accuracy, premature responses, delayed choice, working memory and locomotion measure different functions; an animal task phenotype does not establish a human ADHD diagnosis.'),
 ('Noradrenergic pathways:','In the tested mouse task, LC projections to dorsomedial prefrontal cortex improved distractor resistance, while ventrolateral orbitofrontal targeting reduced premature responses.'),
 ('Thalamic selection:','Prefrontal-dependent reticular modulation changes geniculate inhibition and visual gain according to the selected sensory modality.'),
 ('Receptor and channel context:','Adrenergic and D1 actions can sharpen prefrontal firing at suitable exposure; excessive D1 signaling can suppress delay activity through an HCN-sensitive mechanism.'),
 ('Regional dopamine regulation:','NET contributes to frontal dopamine uptake; DAT deletion prolongs striatal signals, while SHR and Lphn3 models have distinct regional and drug-response profiles.'),
 ('Comparative limits:','Sleep loss weakens fly selection under visual competition, and sleep-related rescue depends on genotype; shared behavioral measures or molecules do not establish identical circuits across species.')]
